8. Current Position

Based on the work completed so far, the current position is:
	•	initial prioritisation is underway
	•	the first cut can be derived from AI use case descriptions and architecture discussions
	•	specific source-level detail is available only for some use cases at this stage
	•	the most immediate priority areas are:
	•	documents
	•	audio/transcripts
	•	chat/conversational logs
	•	enterprise knowledge artefacts
	•	policy/procedure knowledge
	•	customer servicing knowledge

This is sufficient for a first strategic view, but it will need to be refined as discovery continues.

9. Recommendation

The workstream should proceed with the following immediate prioritisation:

Prioritise these unstructured data types first
	•	documents
	•	audio and transcripts
	•	chat and conversational logs
	•	enterprise knowledge artefacts
	•	semi-structured business content

Prioritise these knowledge domains first
	•	policies and procedures / bank operating knowledge
	•	customer interaction and servicing knowledge
	•	enterprise knowledge artefacts

Use this operating approach
	•	classify needs by data type and knowledge domain first
	•	add specific named sources where architecture detail is already available
	•	refine the prioritisation iteratively as use case discovery progresses


10. Next Steps
	1.	Review the current AI use case catalogue and identify which use cases rely on unstructured or semi-structured data.
	2.	Classify each relevant use case by:
	•	priority data type
	•	priority knowledge domain
	•	known source examples
	3.	Extend the source inventory where deeper architecture knowledge already exists.
	4.	Use the output to inform:
	•	source inventory
	•	capability prioritisation
	•	reference architecture
	•	strategic offerings and PoVs


